You can achieve a responsive, auto-wrapping grid without media queries using CSS Grid's `auto-fit` and `minmax()` functions. Here is the standard pattern:

```css
.card-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(250px, 100%), 1fr));
  gap: 1.5rem;
}
```

This setup tells the browser to create as many columns as will fit (`auto-fit`) with a minimum width of `250px` and a maximum of `1fr` (stretching to fill available space). The inner `min(250px, 100%)` prevents the cards from overflowing when the viewport is narrower than 250px, ensuring true responsiveness.
